Attributes
==========

Definition
----------

Attributes are used to:

> Change the default behavior of a field.

* * * * *

Important Note
--------------

Attributes do NOT create fields.

Attributes only modify behavior.

* * * * *

Example 1: Remove Add-Me Icon
=============================

Default Watch List displays:

```
Add Me Icon
```

* * * * *

### Requirement

Hide Add Me icon.

* * * * *

### Attribute

```
no_add_me
```

* * * * *

### Result

Add Me icon disappears.

* * * * *

Example 2: Tree Picker
======================

Default Behavior
----------------

Assignment Group shows:

```
Groups Only
```

* * * * *

Requirement
-----------

Show:

```
Groups+Group Members
```

* * * * *

### Attribute

```
tree_picker
```

* * * * *

### Result

Users can browse both groups and members.

* * * * *

Example 3: Additional User Information
======================================

Default Suggestion
------------------

Displays:

```
NameEmail
```

* * * * *

Requirement
-----------

Display:

```
NameEmailLocationDepartment
```

* * * * *

### Configuration

Use semicolon-separated values.

Example:

```
email;location;department
```

* * * * *

### Result

Suggestions show additional details.

* * * * *

Attributes Syntax Rules
=======================

Adding Multiple Attributes
--------------------------

Use:

```
Comma (,)
```

Example:

```
attribute1,attribute2
```

* * * * *

Adding Additional Display Columns
---------------------------------

Use:

```
Semicolon (;)
```

Example:

```
email;location;department
```

* * * * *

Important Difference
--------------------

### Comma

```
Separate Attributes
```

### Semicolon

```
Separate Display Columns
```

